[{:db/id 17592186338791 :question/worked-solution "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-3x+6\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot x-3+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =2x-3+3{x}^{-1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=4$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=4} & =2(4)-3+3(4)^{-1/2} \\\\  & =8-3+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $\\frac{13}{2}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064259 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0be8176c-dc51-5ee3-ab7e-f7738c95222f" "question-2d253a70-5faa-50fb-9a2a-215f206560d5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0be8176c-dc51-5ee3-ab7e-f7738c95222f" :question/id #uuid "0be8176c-dc51-5ee3-ab7e-f7738c95222f" :question/math-academy-id "q-102233" :question/problem "Find the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y=2{x}^{2}-2$ whose tangent has a slope of $2.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-2.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2x-0 \\\\  & =4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=2$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $2$ at the point where $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-094ecf41-887a-52fa-b0d5-b36a3c36a651"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-094ecf41-887a-52fa-b0d5-b36a3c36a651" :answer-field/id #uuid "094ecf41-887a-52fa-b0d5-b36a3c36a651" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a7446308-87a4-557c-81d1-2285139a39b9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5794d662-7689-53db-beb1-12960e04eb76" "answer-fb519e52-9aba-525a-a842-402c8e22792e" "answer-f094f3a8-968e-548f-a10e-1ed224acebba" "answer-9baf83f0-5754-547b-8165-594f9fd2fc98" "answer-a7446308-87a4-557c-81d1-2285139a39b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5794d662-7689-53db-beb1-12960e04eb76" :answer/id #uuid "5794d662-7689-53db-beb1-12960e04eb76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb519e52-9aba-525a-a842-402c8e22792e" :answer/id #uuid "fb519e52-9aba-525a-a842-402c8e22792e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f094f3a8-968e-548f-a10e-1ed224acebba" :answer/id #uuid "f094f3a8-968e-548f-a10e-1ed224acebba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9baf83f0-5754-547b-8165-594f9fd2fc98" :answer/id #uuid "9baf83f0-5754-547b-8165-594f9fd2fc98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7446308-87a4-557c-81d1-2285139a39b9" :answer/id #uuid "a7446308-87a4-557c-81d1-2285139a39b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2d253a70-5faa-50fb-9a2a-215f206560d5" :question/id #uuid "2d253a70-5faa-50fb-9a2a-215f206560d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-102235" :question/problem "Find the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y={x}^{2}+2x+1$ whose tangent has a slope of $-2.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}+2x+1.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+2x+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =2x+2\\cdot 1+0 \\\\  & =2x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=-2$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+2 & =-2 \\\\ 2x & =-2-2 \\\\ 2x & =-4 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $-2$ at the point where $x=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1a6aec05-611b-57f6-bad9-be06a48060a9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1a6aec05-611b-57f6-bad9-be06a48060a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a6aec05-611b-57f6-bad9-be06a48060a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-299aeade-76b6-5ac3-aa72-60ecdf13731f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9983f911-3be7-5a6a-8784-20b49fb6c9e3" "answer-299aeade-76b6-5ac3-aa72-60ecdf13731f" "answer-4320d5f8-7a4f-596c-be19-d15d507a9187" "answer-0a824279-061f-59cf-8233-230d9112721b" "answer-a7d765ac-42fd-591b-b679-f617197ee035"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9983f911-3be7-5a6a-8784-20b49fb6c9e3" :answer/id #uuid "9983f911-3be7-5a6a-8784-20b49fb6c9e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-299aeade-76b6-5ac3-aa72-60ecdf13731f" :answer/id #uuid "299aeade-76b6-5ac3-aa72-60ecdf13731f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4320d5f8-7a4f-596c-be19-d15d507a9187" :answer/id #uuid "4320d5f8-7a4f-596c-be19-d15d507a9187" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a824279-061f-59cf-8233-230d9112721b" :answer/id #uuid "0a824279-061f-59cf-8233-230d9112721b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7d765ac-42fd-591b-b679-f617197ee035" :answer/id #uuid "a7d765ac-42fd-591b-b679-f617197ee035" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-3569f6ba-b87a-5a2f-8057-ba70663084b5" :activity/id #uuid "3569f6ba-b87a-5a2f-8057-ba70663084b5" :activity/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line Using Differentiation" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050711 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-cdb8e701-19ba-5bf1-ba79-29323210d65f" "step-87574386-7278-5570-801f-5b8e5dcb3e31" "step-ea9c14e4-8840-532c-b073-86c61c6e8b49"] :activity/first-step "step-cdb8e701-19ba-5bf1-ba79-29323210d65f" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-cdb8e701-19ba-5bf1-ba79-29323210d65f" :step/id #uuid "cdb8e701-19ba-5bf1-ba79-29323210d65f" :step/content 17592186338791 :step/next "step-87574386-7278-5570-801f-5b8e5dcb3e31" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-87574386-7278-5570-801f-5b8e5dcb3e31" :step/id #uuid "87574386-7278-5570-801f-5b8e5dcb3e31" :step/content "question-0be8176c-dc51-5ee3-ab7e-f7738c95222f" :step/next "step-ea9c14e4-8840-532c-b073-86c61c6e8b49" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ea9c14e4-8840-532c-b073-86c61c6e8b49" :step/id #uuid "ea9c14e4-8840-532c-b073-86c61c6e8b49" :step/content "question-2d253a70-5faa-50fb-9a2a-215f206560d5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105836 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9d2a01e3-0185-5503-82e9-9d6a8de6c36a" "question-290754c3-90f1-5be3-bcd9-34d500e1127f" "question-90664198-1ae6-5ca3-8d3a-7072c273c129"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105669 :question/worked-solution "The polar equation $r=2a\\cos\\theta$ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(a,0).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=2\\cos\\theta,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na = \\dfrac{2}{2} = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=2\\cos\\theta$ gives a circle of radius $\\left|1\\right| = 1$ centered at the point $(1,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/bc/bc5f763522aec68e97bef90126866fe6b2fe7246560d4dc9ddd2c71a5a524d88.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105758 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-aac4981c-3e93-5227-8d9f-16b46e3776f7" "question-f8583d4e-1a83-5981-bb25-84847566b1c0" "question-9d973ab4-2c91-51a2-bf21-8cc67388babd" "question-e0c88cba-2b84-5672-a20e-1cf48e9f5298" "question-daaf9013-5976-5a1b-a75f-74d8d2c1a5cd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105610 :question/worked-solution "The polar equation $r=2a\\sin\\theta$ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(0,a).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=4\\sin\\theta,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na = \\dfrac{4}{2} = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=4\\sin\\theta$ gives a circle of radius $\\left|2\\right| = 2$ centered at the point $(0,2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/a6/a6a1f74e065f3508c92f8a438eb1830aeb4f877c355cd7779e86183a0da92183.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105759 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-eb541cd2-06d9-513e-814b-43ef4f1b8af7" "question-06dd95dd-7aca-5dd6-bbfa-f6a3626f7868" "question-d345ebc0-fb4a-55bd-95ea-a1eddcced6e5" "question-7fdddd6d-d41d-5369-b195-6ee0cc2418de" "question-e14b9dd2-f663-55f7-a3e0-3b4821a83167"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105611 :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows a circle of radius $|a| = |-4.5|=4.5$ centered at the point $(0,-4.5).$ \n\nIn polar coordinates, the equation of such a circle is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-4.5)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105761 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b69fb899-dda9-520e-9df1-5f655ac32f35" "question-2e8e220e-5d02-535f-8203-20819203c421" "question-5fff1012-20ae-54c4-8327-06d77bbed9eb" "question-0054ec1e-580f-564e-8493-248291e1368b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105613 :question/problem "The polar curve $r=k\\cos\\theta,$ where $k$ is a constant, passes through the point $A$ with Cartesian coordinates $\\left(-\\dfrac72,\\dfrac72\\right).$ What is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the polar coordinates of the point $A.$ The distance from $A$ to the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $A$ lies in the second quadrant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|-\\frac{(\\frac{7}{2})}{(\\frac{7}{2})}| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the polar coordinates of $A$ are $\\left(r, \\theta\\right)=\\left(\\dfrac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}, \\dfrac{3\\pi}{4}\\right).$ \n\nTo find the value of $k$, we substitute the polar coordinates of the point $A$ into the polar equation of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =k\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =k\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\ \\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =k(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ k & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the curve is $r=-7\\cos\\theta,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/8a/8aec18033a85129c44765d2670ebe9c931b0c0186c46b74f9b0ea0ae14028b76.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-9d2a01e3-0185-5503-82e9-9d6a8de6c36a" :question/id #uuid "9d2a01e3-0185-5503-82e9-9d6a8de6c36a" :question/math-academy-id "q-86983" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of the polar curve $r=2.5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(a,0).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=2.5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{2.5}{2}=1.25.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=2.5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|1.25|=1.25$ centered at the point $(1.25,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/11/110736084be735e5e103fe6c541cc3f98140743495cc7d23cbb2242c0eade076.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2094cc0d-ae84-5b8b-a163-f4f82a8b47fa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2094cc0d-ae84-5b8b-a163-f4f82a8b47fa" :answer-field/id #uuid "2094cc0d-ae84-5b8b-a163-f4f82a8b47fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e4f10563-2c3f-5c45-8200-4edcd650eda5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e4f10563-2c3f-5c45-8200-4edcd650eda5" "answer-61e8d881-ba1f-5ceb-b3f3-5e65608dd0b9" "answer-7bac5fbb-2490-53e6-92c7-b61639d48653" "answer-ed58c891-ee8c-5063-a091-2e3c6626f6ae" "answer-759a332a-aacd-5a9b-a528-693432d5769d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4f10563-2c3f-5c45-8200-4edcd650eda5" :answer/id #uuid "e4f10563-2c3f-5c45-8200-4edcd650eda5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/11/110736084be735e5e103fe6c541cc3f98140743495cc7d23cbb2242c0eade076.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61e8d881-ba1f-5ceb-b3f3-5e65608dd0b9" :answer/id #uuid "61e8d881-ba1f-5ceb-b3f3-5e65608dd0b9" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/11/11c04b13e2182d2ea29f2b880f1ec98adce669ece3fda27cbcab3f62bfe468c1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7bac5fbb-2490-53e6-92c7-b61639d48653" :answer/id #uuid "7bac5fbb-2490-53e6-92c7-b61639d48653" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/1e/1ef95d469be1e5c6a327feb54bf2a5716ea134b06efa49007c32ebb1134915b8.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed58c891-ee8c-5063-a091-2e3c6626f6ae" :answer/id #uuid "ed58c891-ee8c-5063-a091-2e3c6626f6ae" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a9/a918435617bd32269f0b53a11adcbebd420a21d4e3661ff35457872554b78652.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-759a332a-aacd-5a9b-a528-693432d5769d" :answer/id #uuid "759a332a-aacd-5a9b-a528-693432d5769d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/d1/d102979e445cad0a12f5eadde35664b21fe298faa7180285f430ad7fffe8ca59.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-290754c3-90f1-5be3-bcd9-34d500e1127f" :question/id #uuid "290754c3-90f1-5be3-bcd9-34d500e1127f" :question/math-academy-id "q-16471" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of the polar curve $r=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $a$ centered at the point $(a,0).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{(-5)}{2}=-\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|-2.5|=2.5$ centered at the point $(-2.5,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/02/02093df668e46e73e5204c8d971d06eb99a2e8ee8d33666573a8bea4b62e890b.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-777fd005-d3df-5442-b39d-a3513e09d75d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-777fd005-d3df-5442-b39d-a3513e09d75d" :answer-field/id #uuid "777fd005-d3df-5442-b39d-a3513e09d75d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f747a858-7973-5073-9861-cb53390dace3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f747a858-7973-5073-9861-cb53390dace3" "answer-ba6b781d-f4d7-5f13-9d93-2848afdf07c6" "answer-cd3f3f92-9bd6-5d89-ae3b-b4218dd8b92d" "answer-5fe84bfa-6f9a-52de-ae68-c99ebec95c69" "answer-1160f38c-bfa8-5ecd-b8c4-38d9798b8df5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f747a858-7973-5073-9861-cb53390dace3" :answer/id #uuid "f747a858-7973-5073-9861-cb53390dace3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/02/02093df668e46e73e5204c8d971d06eb99a2e8ee8d33666573a8bea4b62e890b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba6b781d-f4d7-5f13-9d93-2848afdf07c6" :answer/id #uuid "ba6b781d-f4d7-5f13-9d93-2848afdf07c6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :an