:question/worked-solution "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(0,a).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|\\frac{1}{2}|=0.5$ centered at the point $(0,0.5),$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/c4/c41b20869064a366a1b62d6189d87c540e96196891a8abe1cf9b5c240b52a881.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e7bd8811-1ce1-5810-ae56-aca00bb6d5fa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e7bd8811-1ce1-5810-ae56-aca00bb6d5fa" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7bd8811-1ce1-5810-ae56-aca00bb6d5fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-20ebd374-9729-5bd7-9e85-309bb7ab8be6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d4477801-6f2b-557d-9342-c11d4e311bda" "answer-8c75a3af-26e7-59b9-963f-c87800093b26" "answer-66f3d1d4-66d8-5f9a-85d9-f04895f51e19" "answer-3c6e1933-8b64-56f3-acf6-74760ea3b463" "answer-20ebd374-9729-5bd7-9e85-309bb7ab8be6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4477801-6f2b-557d-9342-c11d4e311bda" :answer/id #uuid "d4477801-6f2b-557d-9342-c11d4e311bda" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/3f/3f36027feea8890a9982e820d1e8f9dc250aceffbbe056b8b0943202d890fe15.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c75a3af-26e7-59b9-963f-c87800093b26" :answer/id #uuid "8c75a3af-26e7-59b9-963f-c87800093b26" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/4d/4d7bdf56b52e5582937bca8fd26fa89f5ed23955b5cd8e789839a8a86d7b53a5.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66f3d1d4-66d8-5f9a-85d9-f04895f51e19" :answer/id #uuid "66f3d1d4-66d8-5f9a-85d9-f04895f51e19" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/80/80869aa27a64197954a24d3dcd756ac6ce405b957b3c3e490cd9e3018384