:answer/id #uuid "6649e667-7698-5ea3-9463-8604cfe2c33d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e48c8dad-ac17-5754-a5c4-9a6aca499939" :answer/id #uuid "e48c8dad-ac17-5754-a5c4-9a6aca499939" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11e015a1-706f-5177-93db-0bf6a2d93adc" :answer/id #uuid "11e015a1-706f-5177-93db-0bf6a2d93adc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-41ff18d2-5493-53b7-9e77-82f1434ea309" :question/id #uuid "41ff18d2-5493-53b7-9e77-82f1434ea309" :question/math-academy-id "q-336712" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that {{field-1}} matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-2}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting {{field-3}} into {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ i.e., by substituting any column $c(t)$ of $Φ$ into the homogeneous system, we get\n\n$$\n{c}^{′}(t)=Ac(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}^{′}(t)$ is the corresponding column of derivatives in $Φ.$ As a result, this means that ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that $Φ\\text{ is a fundamental}$ matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L7},$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Substituting\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φu(t) \\\\  & =Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-066bec05-268d-5397-834c-3e44e338208b" "answer-field-1a63bbb4-ea88-5980-8688-35e082862fe9" "answer-field-a1d82869-ee08-5b8e-bf00-ce54c646f823" "answer-field-ffeb5c19-09f0-5528-a066-b2ec8f17f60c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-066bec05-268d-5397-834c-3e44e338208b" :answer-field/id #uuid "066bec05-268d-5397-834c-3e44e338208b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ea8bf55a-f058-5fdd-972f-dc333a5b367f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-735eed43-4b31-5d90-9a34-2ca221059a28" "answer-ec42e44d-b24c-5c90-a2bd-c598ae24cdcc" "answer-ea8bf55a-f058-5fdd-972f-dc333a5b367f" "answer-0379b0b5-fa6e-560f-a805-6be1158baa43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-735eed43-4b31-5d90-9a34-2ca221059a28" :answer/id #uuid "735eed43-4b31-5d90-9a34-2ca221059a28" :answer