er/value "\\text{L1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-273d4cd2-09eb-568f-b28d-d237b7057b2c" :answer/id #uuid "273d4cd2-09eb-568f-b28d-d237b7057b2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bea06e41-a0fd-5f64-81ed-4cbc5f7f834c" :answer/id #uuid "bea06e41-a0fd-5f64-81ed-4cbc5f7f834c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b07c1742-57f9-5140-847d-5f008bfe2c21" :answer/id #uuid "b07c1742-57f9-5140-847d-5f008bfe2c21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-4de652dc-8dfe-5cf9-94a7-2a0b45eb733b" :activity/id #uuid "4de652dc-8dfe-5cf9-94a7-2a0b45eb733b" :activity/title "Solving Systems of ODEs Using Variation of Parameters" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050355 :activity/course 17592186046645 :activity/steps ["step-c715c357-72dc-5986-b16c-987ebd3618e5" "step-2c2e7d30-c6f5-5cad-87f1-8742a876ba3d" "step-3570a941-938a-5632-bc18-ea2f8f3074a9" "step-060efb46-b822-5dba-9e37-6c83cd83dada" "step-129dd3b0-de6d-5f1e-9fbb-5a9a8c1efa71"] :activity/first-step "step-c715c357-72dc-5986-b16c-987ebd3618e5" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-c715c357-72dc-5986-b16c-987ebd3618e5" :step/id #uuid "c715c357-72dc-5986-b16c-987ebd3618e5" :step/content "question-3ff1006e-e8fc-5000-8f28-c2da87881b92" :step/next "step-2c2e7d30-c6f5-5cad-87f1-8742a876ba3d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2c2e7d30-c6f5-5cad-87f1-8742a876ba3d" :step/id #uuid "2c2e7d30-c6f5-5cad-87f1-8742a876ba3d" :step/content "question-026f1da3-fe0b-5238-91da-8230388ad940" :step/next "step-3570a941-938a-5632-bc18-ea2f8f3074a9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3570a941-938a-5632-bc18-ea2f8f3074a9" :step/id #uuid "3570a941-938a-5632-bc18-ea2f8f3074a9" :step/content 17592186167262 :step/next "step-060efb46-b822-5dba-9e37-6c83cd83dada" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-060efb46-b822-5dba-9e37-6c83cd83dada" :step/id #uuid "060efb46-b822-5dba-9e37-6c83cd83dada" :step/content "question-41ff18d2-5493-53b7-9e77-82f1434ea309" :step/next "step-129dd3b0-de6d-5f1e-9fbb-5a9a8c1efa71" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-129dd3b0-de6d-5f1e-9fbb-5a9a8c1efa71" :step/id #uuid "129dd3b0-de6d-5f1e-9fbb-5a9a8c1efa71" :step/content 17592186311831 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186183733 :answer-field/choices 17592186183734] [:db/retract 17592186183733 :answer-field/choices 17592186183735] [:db/retract 17592186183733 :answer-field/choices 17592186183736] [:db/retract 17592186183733 :answer-field/choices 17592186183737] [:db/retract 17592186183733 :answer-field/choices 17592186183738] {:db/id 17592186184854 :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRound the answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}25 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 25\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}25 \\\\ 25\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}25 \\\\ 25\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$  \n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}x}{‖x‖‖{\\text{proj}}_{S}x‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 7+(-1)\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{5}^{2}}\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{50}{\\sqrt{75}\\sqrt{50}} \\\\  & =\\frac{25\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{25\\cdot 3}\\sqrt{25\\cdot 2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}})≈{35.26}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186183733 :answer-field/correct "answer-74f4a2cb-ada9-59ce-9232-893fc30f6270" :answer-field/choices ["answer-01b68167-5d52-5d4b-9b34-1ad51d78353a" "answer-98ceee4f-999c-539a-8b89-18a78e723c35" "answer-74f4a2cb-ada9-59ce-9232-893fc30f6270" "answer-f4fc2e2d-62af-5717-b6ba-70d80cc69eba" "answer-cced283f-45bb-598e-8543-355ab99c0f0c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01b68167-5d52-5d4b-9b34-1ad51d78353a" :answer/id #uuid "01b68167-5d52-5d4b-9b34-1ad51d78353a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{26.53}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98ceee4f-999c-539a-8b89-18a78e723c35" :answer/id #uuid "98ceee4f-999c-539a-8b89-18a78e723c35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{32.56}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74f4a2cb-ada9-59ce-9232-893fc30f6270" :answer/id #uuid "74f4a2cb-ada9-59ce-9232-893fc30f6270" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{35.26}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4fc2e2d-62af-5717-b6ba-70d80cc69eba" :answer/id #uuid "f4fc2e2d-62af-5717-b6ba-70d80cc69eba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{53.26}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cced283f-45bb-598e-8543-355ab99c0f0c" :answer/id #uuid "cced283f-45bb-598e-8543-355ab99c0f0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{56.32}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-e06dfd27-c5ce-573f-9478-c62b9b7844d3" :activity/id #uuid "e06dfd27-c5ce-573f-9478-c62b9b7844d3" :activity/title "Projecting Vectors Onto Subspaces in Euclidean Spaces (Arbitrary Bases): Applications" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048506 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-3f9b4ea0-f09a-5ee5-a1cd-f0cced59a020" "step-59c27f3e-ad1e-56f1-b455-4dfb9b97cba7" "step-f19b9ebd-da07-5de7-a32c-9429d121b85e" "step-459af5b1-8086-5825-86f4-6462d6e52085" "step-e7aa5054-2c6b-5a4a-89a5-81bfccf2db68"] :activity/first-step "step-3f9b4ea0-f09a-5ee5-a1cd-f0cced59a020" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-3f9b4ea0-f09a-5ee5-a1cd-f0cced59a020" :step/id #uuid "3f9b4ea0-f09a-5ee5-a1cd-f0cced59a020" :step/content 17592186184778 :step/next "step-59c27f3e-ad1e-56f1-b455-4dfb9b97cba7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-59c27f3e-ad1e-56f1-b455-4dfb9b97cba7" :step/id #uuid "59c27f3e-ad1e-56f1-b455-4dfb9b97cba7" :step/content 17592186326865 :step/next "step-f19b9ebd-da07-5de7-a32c-9429d121b85e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f19b9ebd-da07-5de7-a32c-9429d121b85e" :step/id #uuid "f19b9ebd-da07-5de7-a32c-9429d121b85e" :step/content 17592186351522 :step/next "step-459af5b1-8086-5825-86f4-6462d6e52085" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-459af5b1-8086-5825-86f4-6462d6e52085" :step/id #uuid "459af5b1-8086-5825-86f4-6462d6e52085" :step/content 17592186184854 :step/next "step-e7aa5054-2c6b-5a4a-89a5-81bfccf2db68" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e7aa5054-2c6b-5a4a-89a5-81bfccf2db68" :step/id #uuid "e7aa5054-2c6b-5a4a-89a5-81bfccf2db68" :step/content 17592186416356 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166746 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0fcd3eab-4854-55ff-b2c1-1082ea396d46" "question-c8776b39-34f7-5d7c-be21-f79bcc825464"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0fcd3eab-4854-55ff-b2c1-1082ea396d46" :question/id #uuid "0fcd3eab-4854-55ff-b2c1-1082ea396d46" :question/math-academy-id "q-90672" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-14,-12],$ find $\\text{Var}[X].$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-14$ and $b=-12.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(-12-(-14))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{4}{12}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3992d953-1244-5557-9945-0b791a18deb7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3992d953-1244-5557-9945-0b791a18deb7" :answer-field/id #uuid "3992d953-1244-5557-9945-0b791a18deb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-94db1437-5e1a-57d2-8107-cd2b1bc91e9a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bcc9ba8c-57a5-5728-b63d-c0258bfc7f44" "answer-580b19f4-06cd-5f23-8232-395131ef6d7b" "answer-a6355efe-d532-5cd4-af35-a010ccf31b0b" "answer-94db1437-5e1a-57d2-8107-cd2b1bc91e9a" "answer-8a00859d-461d-5c26-a897-6628f10261bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcc9ba8c-57a5-5728-b63d-c0258bfc7f44" :answer/id #uuid "bcc9ba8c-57a5-5728-b63d-c0258bfc7f44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-580b19f4-06cd-5f23-8232-395131ef6d7b" :answer/id #uuid "580b19f4-06cd-5f23-8232-395131ef6d7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6355efe-d532-5cd4-af35-a010ccf31b0b" :answer/id #uuid "a6355efe-d532-5cd4-af35-a010ccf31b0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94db1437-5e1a-57d2-8107-cd2b1bc91e9a" :answer/id #uuid "94db1437-5e1a-57d2-8107-cd2b1bc91e9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a00859d-461d-5c26-a897-6628f10261bc" :answer/id #uuid "8a00859d-461d-5c26-a897-6628f10261bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166794 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-da016258-0a74-55d6-826a-b4bf1b04b20f" "question-e2d806a2-2942-5a78-912e-4a549e08c6e1" "question-b5a32830-d248-5fc8-bc7e-b05512cbde4a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-da016258-0a74-55d6-826a-b4bf1b04b20f" :question/id #uuid "da016258-0a74-55d6-826a-b4bf1b04b20f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96543" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-1,5],$ find $\\text{SD}[X].$ Round your answer to three decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-1$ and $b=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(5-(-1))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{36}{12}=3.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{3}≈1.732.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-27ef2412-e3b2-5d7b-90bb-7eff3b5943a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-27ef2412-e3b2-5d7b-90bb-7eff3b5943a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "27ef2412-e3b2-5d7b-90bb-7eff3b5943a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-494e131c-f649-5ebc-ad15-3ca3db67e9c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-576b71e1-7f62-56c3-a6d4-b905df0183d1" "answer-494e131c-f649-5ebc-ad15-3ca3db67e9c4" "answer-1585b6e2-429d-51d8-8c0e-3911e7716053" "answer-70098b3e-4590-5b38-a9c2-71c3acb1c70b" "answer-c7ed1bc3-120f-5883-a357-b19fb6040732"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-576b71e1-7f62-56c3-a6d4-b905df0183d1" :answer/id #uuid "576b71e1-7f62-56c3-a6d4-b905df0183d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.722" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-494e131c-f649-5ebc-ad15-3ca3db67e9c4" :answer/id #uuid "494e131c-f649-5ebc-ad15-3ca3db67e9c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.732" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1585b6e2-429d-51d8-8c0e-3911e7716053" :answer/id #uuid "1585b6e2-429d-51d8-8c0e-3911e7716053" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.737" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70098b3e-4590-5b38-a9c2-71c3acb1c70b" :answer/id #uuid "70098b3e-4590-5b38-a9c2-71c3acb1c70b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.237" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7ed1bc3-120f-5883-a357-b19fb6040732" :answer/id #uuid "c7ed1bc3-120f-5883-a357-b19fb6040732" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.702" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e2d806a2-2942-5a78-912e-4a549e08c6e1" :question/id #uuid "e2d806a2-2942-5a78-912e-4a549e08c6e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-96563" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-15,-8],$ find $\\text{SD}[X].$ Round your answer to three decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-15$ and $b=-8.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(-8-(-15))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{49}{12}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{12}}=\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{6}≈2.021.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1df1aa21-3031-5917-aa7a-0e2c69c11c86"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1df1aa21-3031-5917-aa7a-0e2c69c11c86" :answer-field/id #uuid "1df1aa21-3031-5917-aa7a-0e2c69c11c86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e75fd171-e5cc-55b8-910f-afdfe76603ad" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1de0e48a-1c15-541b-8c3d-0a796ba76229" "answer-9bac3d75-a967-5c99-b769-8dad1d46751e" "answer-e75fd171-e5cc-55b8-910f-afdfe76603ad" "answer-9d84f3f9-b228-59a5-b0a4-f1927cbf07ec" "answer-27fbf980-3763-53bc-b7f2-b9c877a749dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1de0e48a-1c15-541b-8c3d-0a796ba76229" :answer/id #uuid "1de0e48a-1c15-541b-8c3d-0a796ba76229" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.122" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bac3d75-a967-5c99-b769-8dad1d46751e" :answer/id #uuid "9bac3d75-a967-5c99-b769-8dad1d46751e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.221" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e75fd171-e5cc-55b8-910f-afdfe76603ad" :answer/id #uuid "e75fd171-e5cc-55b8-910f-afdfe76603ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.021" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d84f3f9-b228-59a5-b0a4-f1927cbf07ec" :answer/id #uuid "9d84f3f9-b228-59a5-b0a4-f1927cbf07ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.022" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27fbf980-3763-53bc-b7f2-b9c877a749dc" :answer/id #uuid "27fbf980-3763-53bc-b7f2-b9c877a749dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.201" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c8776b39-34f7-5d7c-be21-f79bcc825464" :question/id #uuid "c8776b39-34f7-5d7c-be21-f79bcc825464" :question/math-academy-id "q-130712" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-8,1],$ find $\\text{Var}[X].$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-8$ and $b=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(1-(-8))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{81}{12}=\\frac{27}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-48c440fe-ee45-50ad-96dc-aebf71a08eee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-48c440fe-ee45-50ad-96dc-aebf71a08eee" :answer-field/id #uuid "48c440fe-ee45-50ad-96dc-aebf71a08eee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-063be259-5820-5ee3-a0a9-153a9190b3b1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c3a5cc7a-a7bb-5977-b0ca-f4be409679db" "answer-063be259-5820-5ee3-a0a9-153a9190b3b1" "answer-cc0df2f6-7d00-502e-aec5-aa25d1b1c455" "answer-49619131-cc7e-5068-b060-d49334625ec4" "answer-168d8c47-f103-5ff2-a22e-8cbcced9dcc4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3a5cc7a-a7bb-5977-b0ca-f4be409679db" :answer/id #uuid "c3a5cc7a-a7bb-5977-b0ca-f4be409679db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-063be259-5820-5ee3-a0a9-153a9190b3b1" :answer/id #uuid "063be259-5820-5ee3-a0a9-153a9190b3b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc0df2f6-7d00-502e-aec5-aa25d1b1c455" :answer/id #uuid "cc0df2f6-7d00-502e-aec5-aa25d1b1c455" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49619131-cc7e-5068-b060-d49334625ec4" :answer/id #uuid "49619131-cc7e-5068-b060-d49334625ec4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-168d8c47-f103-5ff2-a22e-8cbcced9dcc4" :answer/id #uuid "168d8c47-f103-5ff2-a22e-8cbcced9dcc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b5a32830-d248-5fc8-bc7e-b05512cbde4a" :question/id #uuid "b5a32830-d248-5fc8-bc7e-b05512cbde4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130714" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[3,8],$ find $\\text{SD}[X].$ Round your answer to three decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=3$ and $b=8.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(8-3)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{25}{12}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{12}}=\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{6}≈1.443.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-01db84db-d17a-5436-857c-df53b3ee501f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-01db84db-d17a-5436-857c-df53b3ee501f" :answer-field/id #uuid "01db84db-d17a-5436-857c-df53b3ee501f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-55a4d135-b137-503e-9c19-b69e506a0e8b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-267ab761-26d7-57dc-8def-97aa5d384c1c" "answer-55a4d135-b137-503e-9c19-b69e506a0e8b" "answer-40ad5a30-1983-5ba4-9063-ee1cc2b79f04" "answer-b372d906-77f5-592d-9cee-5d9413f82f70" "answer-49b53d5f-2296-55f1-9cb6-bf7bb6bfc356"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-267ab761-26d7-57dc-8def-97aa5d384c1c" :answer/id #uuid "267ab761-26d7-57dc-8def-97aa5d384c1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.128" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55a4d135-b137-503e-9c19-b69e506a0e8b" :answer/id #uuid "55a4d135-b137-503e-9c19-b69e506a0e8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.443" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40ad5a30-1983-5ba4-9063-ee1cc2b79f04" :answer/id #uuid "40ad5a30-1983-5ba4-9063-ee1cc2b79f04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.713" :db/ensure 